WEBVTT

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.320
I reached a decision...

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:24.110
That I would surely make your wish come true myself."

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:31.300
Hozuki-chan, we'll soon be arriving at our destination in the Libyan Desert.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.060
The sixth

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.010
and final sketch.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:53.610
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:53.610
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:01.410
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:01.410
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:08.670
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:08.670
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.750
shinkuromanika

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.750
Synchromanica

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.300
itsu no ma ni ka

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.300
Before I know it

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.470
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.470
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:21.760
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:21.760
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:28.270
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:28.270
I can hear someone's dream

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:35.240
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:35.240
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:48.040
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:48.040
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.380
shinkuromanika

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.380
Synchromanica

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:54.510
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:54.510
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.550
shinkuromanika

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.550
Synchromanica

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.770
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.770
The synchrony of your life

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:10.100
Space-Time Goldfish
(Part 1)

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:23.210
Oh, here it is.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.130
Great! The sixth sketch!

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:31.170
What... is this?

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.120
A telescope?

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:35.890
What's going on?

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.340
Hozuki-chan, may I?

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:44.560
Well?

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.390
It's just a telescope.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.810
Why does the sixth one come with a telescope?

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.570
What do you think, Hocchibi?

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:55.840
Anna-san...

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.070
Yes, that's right...

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.540
The sixth sketch should be in Libya.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.330
We should have the entire set by tomorrow evening.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.240
I understand.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.050
What should we do with this piece of junk?

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:18.970
Toss it?

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:20.300
We can't do that.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.320
It has too much historical value to not take it with us.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:25.680
But it's just a telescope.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.360
So, we now have all of the sketches.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.690
Have we learned anything from them?

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.530
Anna-san...

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.320
What?

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:44.170
You said that there was a total of seven sketches before.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:46.620
Oh, that...

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.330
Didn't I mention that was likely just
unsubstantiated speculation on my part?

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.460
Really?

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.330
Y-Yes.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.590
Anna-san, there's something I want to ask you—

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.920
Enemy attack! Enemy attack!

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.260
Why? What's happening?

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:07.890
We gave that spoiled brat the hourglass,
and we've reached an understanding with the air pirates!

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:10.770
Did he figure it out?

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:14.940
The enemy is approaching at high speed and is nearly on top of us!

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.560
Also, I'm pretty much running on empty!

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.980
Huh? What do you mean?

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.280
How did they know where to find us?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.200
I mean, who's coming, anyway?

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.320
I knew it was the spoiled brat.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.150
Why? <i>Why</i> is he still after us?

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:04.060
Hocchii, can we take off?

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.780
We're out of fuel...

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:07.210
Seriously?

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:10.280
I told you I was running on empty!

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.320
I'd like to discuss something, Galileo sisters.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:47.440
I have no use for imitations.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:51.710
What do you mean by "imitation?"

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.410
Allow me to cut to the chase.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:58.500
Give me all of the sketches that you've collected.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.720
You <i>do</i> have all of them, yes?

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:06.700
This beautiful Libyan Desert is where you found the sixth.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.680
I've been waiting until now.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.470
You'll let us go free if we do?

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.640
And what if we refuse?

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:16.250
Refuse?

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:21.400
I had always considered you to be the intelligent child.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:24.610
After all, you built that thing entirely on your own.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.150
It's quite impressive.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.740
However, that seems to be the extent of your abilities.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:34.370
Suppose that the sketches contain
information about a new energy source

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.290
capable of saving the world.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.750
Even if you, Hozuki Ferrari,

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.790
were allowed to analyze it, so what?

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:45.460
A certain degree of funding and infrastructure is necessary

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:48.880
to use that information to generate vast amounts of energy.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.690
I know that!

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:53.100
But even so, I won't give it to you!

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:54.650
Listen well:

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:58.600
the laws of physics, mathematics, formulae and numbers

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.890
allow you to derive answers

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:05.610
despite the fact that you are merely a child.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:10.200
But in this world, some things cannot be learned through books.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.350
Do you know what they are?

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:17.650
Experience can only be gained through hardship and despair.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:22.590
You are a child. You know nothing.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.520
Given our current situation,

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:28.630
if I were in your position

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:32.840
I would hand over the sketches without any hesitation at all.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.850
As well as the Galileo Tesoro you swapped out.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.980
Give him the sketches.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.310
Anna-san?

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:47.770
Your lives are worth more than the sketches.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:48.900
But...

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.520
You can drop the act now, Anna.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.410
Act?

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:57.200
I don't understand... Please explain, Anna-san!

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.240
I am...

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:01.120
Messier's spy.

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:06.630
I got close to you three in order to ensure that you found the Moon sketches.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.440
You never noticed?

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:10.550
Jeez.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.420
As Galileo's descendants,

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.880
I'm surprised it took you this long to find them.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:18.530
But you're all selfish and can't ever get along.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:21.430
I tire of your constant bickering.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.430
So stupid.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:25.770
Looking at you,

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:29.320
I'm glad I don't have any sisters.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:30.900
That's mean.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:32.820
I thought so...

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:35.520
Hocchii...

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:39.870
You dumped the <i>Galileo</i>'s fuel, didn't you?

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:41.160
That's right.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:44.080
You're lying, aren't you? Anna-san?

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:45.830
Enough! You three sicken me!

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:50.880
The sketches are all you came for, right?

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.210
Then you can just let the girls—

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:53.590
I'm afraid not.

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.680
They know far too much.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:00.970
R-Roberto?

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:05.610
You may finish them off.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.320
What's the matter, Anna?

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:13.550
Hurry.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:17.950
Anna-san!

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:18.780
Go!

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.030
But...

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.790
Just go!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.950
The fuel is still in the engine room!

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.450
Anna...

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.920
You've become a wonderful woman.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:41.470
Now's our chance!

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:51.900
It's that violent bastard in the iron mask!

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:55.400
Maybe he's like you, boss, chasing a girl—

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.490
Don't even joke about that.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:01.200
In any case, just protect Bambina and her sisters from that crazy bastard!

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:05.500
For the moment, we are no longer air pirates! You got that?

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:06.490
Got it!

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.390
Damn it!

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:22.760
I will protect you!

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:26.100
We're going to get blown to pieces before we can even reach the ship!

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.020
Just run!

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.730
Are you guys okay?

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.010
I'm okay!

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:39.990
Hocchibi, what is that?

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.990
The real Galileo Tesoro.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.210
When did you even manage to swap it?

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:46.500
Then Picco Rosso was a mecha, too?

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:51.960
We're finished!

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.790
What's going on?

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:08.950
What?

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:10.930
I'm gonna fall!

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:23.010
Ow...

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:30.310
Hey, stop! D-Don't struggle!

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:47.780
Where am I?

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.790
Where the heck did you come from?

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:55.790
It's so warm...

00:12:57.890 --> 00:13:00.710
For six months I've poured my money and materials into this plane...

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.880
It's been through countless trials, errors and refinements

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:07.610
only to be reduced to a pile of rubble the day it was finally finished!

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:10.180
Hey, you!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.790
What're you going to do about this, huh?!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.100
Oh, um, I mean...

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:27.000
One, two, three, four, five...

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.200
There it goes again.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:37.270
Did you just fall from those clouds?

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.300
I... I'm not sure.

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:42.090
I think what happened was...

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.420
What's going on?

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.940
Haa-nee, Kaa-nee... What should I do?

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:55.810
What do I do?

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.020
C-Calm down.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:58.850
I have to get back or—

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:03.320
If you fell here from those clouds,

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:07.860
I've deduced that the same phenomenon
will occur within twenty-three days!

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:08.860
Huh?

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:13.490
Regardless, you'll need the <i>Galileo</i>.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.580
I'll make repairs.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.620
You should help, as well.

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:18.500
The <i>Galileo</i>?

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:20.450
Yes.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:24.380
The first, and most memorable,
experimental craft built by Galileo Galilei.

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.620
<i>You're</i> Galileo Galilei?

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:30.720
Then I'm in...

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.620
This feels great.

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:45.230
I've never felt such a warm breeze before.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:49.200
Come to think of it, I never asked your name.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:52.380
I'm Hozuki... Hozuki Ferrari.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:54.760
That's...

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:00.710
I still can't believe it,

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.210
but there's no doubt that I'm in...

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:07.710
I've observed clouds like the ones today multiple times.

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:11.440
The townsfolk fear them as omens of misfortune,

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:15.390
and they shut themselves within their homes when they appear.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:20.690
Having never seen such clouds before, I simply continued my observations.

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:24.640
And one day, strange objects like these began to fall from them...

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:34.510
I have no idea what they are, nor from whence they come.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.640
However, if it fell from those clouds,

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.750
it must be related to that light.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.490
That's only speculation, though.

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:45.960
The light...

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.690
According to my observations...

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:52.340
The objects only fell when the light flashed with its greatest frequency.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:56.470
The light was very intense at these times, as well.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:59.190
Following that, the flashing would gradually slow,

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:02.950
the light would dim, and the clouds
themselves would eventually vanish.

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:07.050
This graph depicts the interval between the light flashing

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:08.610
and the clouds vanishing.

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:14.110
So if you enter the clouds at this time, you should be able to return home.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:15.510
Okay...

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:19.240
All right, then... Let's get started.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:23.990
Although, what could I ask an amateur like you to do?

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:37.470
Um...

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:39.890
May I?

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:40.970
What?

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.390
H-Hey!

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:47.830
I think doing this here will improve efficiency.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:53.400
Th-This is...

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:55.410
What do you think?

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:57.810
Wow! It's amazing!

00:16:57.810 --> 00:17:02.000
This will let me increase the wingspan and maximize lift!

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:05.250
This is excellent, Hozuki, despite how small you are!

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:08.080
Huh? Small?

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:19.160
Let's use this for a practice run.

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:21.950
So we're just watching for any issues?

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:22.830
Right.

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:26.790
Everything must be tested, observed and proven.

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:29.790
We'll test this first thing tomorrow.

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:30.790
Okay.

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:36.710
Here.

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:38.790
Th-Thanks...

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:44.310
I... I wonder if tomorrow will be sunny.

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:46.310
I hope so.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:08.340
I don't usually bring rain with me...

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:09.830
It's your fault!

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.210
Huh? Why?

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:14.540
You made this creepy doll, didn't you?

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:17.090
Hey!

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:20.090
I went to all the trouble to make it,
and you just took it down?!

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:24.050
Don't hang something so creepy in my home without asking.

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:25.600
That's uncalled for...

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:27.970
It's called a "Teru Teru Bouzu."

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.350
It's a really old Japanese tradition.

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:34.020
They're charms that ensure sunny weather if they're hung by the window.

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:36.020
This?

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:39.030
It looks cursed to me.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:43.320
Besides, do you really believe in something so unscientific?

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:46.500
That's the entire point of charms!

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.160
I don't get it.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:53.040
The rain doesn't look likely to let up.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:54.290
Yeah...

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:57.110
I wonder if that cloud will appear again.

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:02.050
I wonder if I can get back...

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.760
Don't worry.

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:09.600
That cloud will come again for sure.

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:12.280
Trust me.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:14.810
Okay.

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:17.230
Thanks.

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:51.750
You're just like Haa-nee!

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:13.200
It stopped raining.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:14.090
Yeah...

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:41.110
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:41.110
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:44.940
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:44.940
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:51.950
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:51.950
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:57.080
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:57.080
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:01.460
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:01.460
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:06.760
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:06.760
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:14.720
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:14.720
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:23.110
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:23.110
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:30.240
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:30.240
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:42.380
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:42.380
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
